%% EasyInvio repository architecture, 18 October 2026.
flowchart TB
    Web[Single-page web workspace] --> Auth[JWT / membership / tenant / role guards]
    WhatsApp[Signed Twilio WhatsApp] --> Bind[Verified phone binding or opt-in onboarding]
    Bind --> Gateway[Shared conversational gateway]
    Web --> Gateway
    Auth --> API[FastAPI routers / lifespan / async services]
    Gateway --> API
    Hooks[Verified carrier, store and Stripe callbacks] --> API
    API --> Rating[Deterministic rating / margin / top-ten consolidation]
    API --> Booking[PartnerLifecycleService / FinanceEngine]
    API --> Ops[Catalogs / dispatch / tracking / support / audits]
    API -. optional .-> Agents[Bounded supervisor and typed AI workers]
    Agents -. advisory only .-> Rating
    Agents --> RAG[Published help corpus / local vectors / citations]
    Rating --> Carriers[EasyPost / Sendcloud / Shippo]
    Booking --> Carriers
    Booking --> Stripe[Stripe Checkout / verified payment events]
    Ops --> Providers[Configured stores / CRM / insurance / tariff services]
    Booking --> DB[(Supabase PostgreSQL / wallet locks / ledger)]
    Ops --> DB
    Gateway --> DB
    DB --> Jobs[Durable SQL jobs / outboxes / reconciliation]
    Jobs --> Providers
    Agents --> OpenAI[OpenAI structured outputs / embeddings]
    RAG --> Docs[Local Help Centre guides]
    Bind --> SupabaseAuth[Supabase Auth + custom SMTP for email codes]
